id: pm-cstuys
title: "GH-868: atomic replacement contract for linked files and docs"
description: "Update supports atomic replace modes for tests and dependencies but rejects clearing and adding linked files or docs in one mutation. Add typed replace-files and replace-docs contracts across SDK, CLI, MCP, completions, history, and rollback behavior."
type: Issue
status: in_progress
priority: 1
tags[7]: "area:cli","area:mcp","area:sdk",atomicity,github-report,linked-resources,mutation-contract
created_at: "2026-08-02T06:48:34.624Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-02T11:35:45.255Z"
assignee: "harness:codex"
claim_principal: "harness:codex#b54ea3df17a9d4f6f64078c0"
author: "harness:codex"
acceptance_criteria: "Update accepts typed atomic replace-files and replace-docs inputs; CLI, SDK, MCP schemas, completions, and help expose the same contract; Replacement writes one history transition and cannot leave an intermediate empty set; Empty replacement and rollback behavior are tested; The GitHub report is linked to this canonical PM item"
goal: project management = context management
objective: Agents can correct complete evidence sets atomically through public SDK primitives
value: Interrupted evidence maintenance cannot leave partial project context
impact: Brings files and docs to mutation parity with tests and dependencies
outcome: A single SDK/CLI action deterministically replaces linked evidence collections
why_now: GitHub #868 identified the parity gap on 2026.8.2
parent: pm-usfg
risk: medium
confidence: high
reporter: GitHub #868
severity: medium
expected_result: Files and docs can be atomically replaced
actual_result: Clear plus add is rejected and no replacement mode exists
affected_version: 2026.8.2
component: item update SDK/CLI/MCP contracts
regression: false
