comments[6]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-02T06:48:34.624Z","harness:codex","Duplicate check evidence: searched all open, closed, and canceled PM items for replace-files, replace-docs, atomic linked-resource replacement, and clear-plus-add. Closed pm-bjpo owns linked-test replacement only; no item owns files/docs parity. Source: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/issues/868."
  "2026-08-02T07:13:25.024Z","harness:codex","Implementation evidence: update and update-many now atomically replace files/docs with pre-mutation conflict/value validation, ownership bypass restrictions, legacy-none normalization parity, typed option contracts, documentation, and regression coverage."
  "2026-08-02T07:22:06.399Z","harness:codex","Manual acceptance caught an argv-bootstrap parity gap before shipment: Commander exposed --replace-files/--replace-docs but the guarded canonical flag vocabulary did not. Added both update/update-many flag contracts and a subprocess CLI regression so typo correction cannot intercept valid replacement flags."
  "2026-08-02T07:23:02.567Z","harness:codex","Manual isolated acceptance: dist CLI accepted --replace-files and --replace-docs together for temp item pm-d2xt and authoritative get returned only src/replaced.ts and docs/replaced.md. This proves guarded argv parsing plus atomic storage behavior outside the repository tracker."
  "2026-08-02T11:28:18.862Z","harness:codex","Repository-wide verification: 418 test files and 6,703 tests passed under the sandboxed coverage runner with exact 100% statements (47,529/47,529), branches (34,246/34,246), functions (9,673/9,673), and lines (46,119/46,119). No coverage thresholds, exclusions, or ignore counts were weakened."
  "2026-08-02T11:35:45.255Z","harness:codex","Packed-consumer acceptance: pnpm smoke:npx passed the generated tarball across 15 packaged modules. An independent tarball was then installed from unrelated root /tmp/tmp.0PKR29g4Dz into separate npm and Bun consumers with isolated project/global trackers; both initialized, created items, added evidence, and returned files lookup total=1. npm additionally proved atomic files/docs replacement and exact repeated evidence changed=false."
